{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","externalID":"PostHogEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"PostHogEncoding"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s "},{"code":"\/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"). A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"type":"text","text":". The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and the like)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, and one too large for PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event limit. The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/docume